ISO-10303-21;
/* Twi050: Two ADVANCED_FACEs on PLANEs; both outer EDGE_LOOPs reference the same VERTEX_POINT instance at (0,0,0); sender deduplicated vertices too aggressively — (0,0,0) appears in face-0 and face-1 wires as the exact same entity reference; the shared VERTEX_POINT IS the mechanism; all EDGE_CURVEs ARE wired into EDGE_LOOPs → FACE_OUTER_BOUNDs → ADVANCED_FACEs in a CLOSED_SHELL — never orphaned; kernel must detect vertex over-sharing and split into independent copies, one per wire, or reject as malformed */
